<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The launcher's network security config (design 102 D15 (a), the user's decision of 2026-11-15; before it security
  review S-M1's of 2026-11-04).
  - Cleartext is allowed app-wide: the Wi-Fi sign-in window (portal/, process :portal) must load a captive portal, which
    is http by nature (Android's probe URL, the intercepted redirect, portals on IP literals), and a config names hosts,
    never address ranges. The server path stays https by code - serverUrlVerdict and ServerTransport refuse a plain-http
    server address (but to a Tailscale IP literal) before the bearer or a socket, pinned by the shared vectors
    (server_url_vectors.json) - and every other client is https by code; ServerTransportTest's source scan fails the
    build on a new HTTP client anywhere else, and a new library's own HTTP is caught by the dependency review
    (gradle/verification-metadata.xml).
  - Only the system's CAs are trusted (never a user-installed one).
  - tailnet-server.vibb.invalid stays named (server/ServerTransport.kt, TAILNET_SERVER_HOST): the tailnet client gives
    OkHttp that name for a server at http://<tailnet IP>, and only that client resolves it, through tsnet's proxy.
  The debug build's copy (src/debug/res/xml/) also trusts user CAs, in a debug build only. ServerTransportTest pins both and the
  manifest's reference.
-->
<network-security-config xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" tools:ignore="InsecureBaseConfiguration">
        <trust-anchors>
            <certificates src="system" />
        </trust-anchors>
    </base-config>
    <domain-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true">
        <domain includeSubdomains="false">tailnet-server.vibb.invalid</domain>
    </domain-config>
</network-security-config>
